Presidential elections were held in [[Cyprus]] on 7 February 1993, with a second round on 14 February.<ref name=NS>[[Dieter Nohlen]] & Philip Stöver (2010) ''Elections in Europe: A data handbook'', p438 {{ISBN|978-3-8329-5609-7}}</ref> The result was a victory for  [[Glafcos Clerides]] of the [[Democratic Rally]] after he finished as runner-up behind [[George Vassiliou]], supported by [[Progressive Party of Working People|AKEL]], in the first round, a reverse of the [[1988 Cypriot presidential election|1988 elections]]. Voter turnout was 92.4% in the first round and 93.3% in the second.<ref>Nohlen & Stöver, p446</ref>

